    <bpmn:process id="W_W3214" name="W3214. Insurance, Bonding &amp; Contractor Risk Transfer" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New MSA (W3213); renewal; loss event
Frequency: Per MSA + annual verification
Volume: ~30–60 contractors
Owner: Risk &amp; Insurance Manager
Participants: Risk &amp; Insurance Mgr (links to VS-26), Legal, Safety (links to VS-24), Procurement, Agency/Insurer
Source: workflow W3214 — Insurance, Bonding &amp; Contractor Risk Transfer</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3214_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3214_Lane1" name="Risk &amp; Insurance Mgr">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3214_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3214_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3214_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3214_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3214_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3214_Start3" name="New MSA (W3213); renewal; loss event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3214_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3214_Task4" name="Risk &amp; Insurance Mgr define risk-transfer requirements per category…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Risk &amp; Insurance Mgr define risk-transfer requirements per category: contractor&#x27;s general liability, employer&#x27;s liability/workers&#x27; compensation (ECC coverage for their employees), professional indemnity (IT/engineering), third-party property damage, fidelity bond (for cash-handling security), motor (for delivery); set limits, deductibles, BuildRight as additional insured
Responsible (R): Risk &amp; Insurance Mgr / Legal
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per category</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3214_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3214_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3214_Task5" name="Require and verify certificates of insurance (COI) before engagement and at…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Require and verify certificates of insurance (COI) before engagement and at renewal; verify authenticity with insurer; track expiry and renewals; enforce remediation for lapsed/non-compliant coverage (suspend engagement)
Responsible (R): Risk &amp; Insurance Mgr / Procurement
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3214_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3214_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3214_Task6" name="Manage claims involving contractors: incident response (W3228), coverage…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Manage claims involving contractors: incident response (W3228), coverage invocation, subrogation where BuildRight not at fault, deductible/allocation; lessons feed risk register (links to VS-21.2) and contract terms (W3213)
Responsible (R): Risk &amp; Insurance Mgr / Legal
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3214_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3214_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3214_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3214_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3214_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-121 (ensure lawful contracting &amp; worker classification.) | - operational: COI verification and suspension-for-noncompliance; operational: category-specific limit setting
Owner: Risk &amp; Insurance Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
